+  // Diagnostic-only write-before-read contract probe (poison build; never
+  // deployable). When VLLM_XPU_GDN_SPEC_SCRATCH_POISON names a field group
+  // (or "all"), the named spec scratch buffers are filled with hostile
+  // sentinels BEFORE the spec kernels run, in both the persistent and
+  // per-call branches. If every field honors write-before-read, outputs are
+  // unaffected; any read of a poisoned value produces NaN garbage (float)
+  // or an invalid state slot (int), localizing the violating field group.
+  // has_initial_state and exact_query_start_loc are excluded: their
